  "id": "614870",
  "subject": [],
  "title": "Trikomia 3",
  "provenance": "Barrington Atlas: BAtlas 62  Trikomia 3",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/unlocated",
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/settlement"
  ],
  "details": "<p>Ptolemy places this Trikomia in \u03a6\u03c1\u03c5\u03b3\u03af\u03b1 \u039c\u03b5\u03b3\u1f00\u03bb\u03b7\u03c2 (Greater Phrygia), listing it between <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../609473\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">\u039c\u03b9\u03b4\u03ac\u03ca\u03bf\u03bd (Midaion)</a> and <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../619103\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">\u1f0c\u03b3\u03ba\u03c5\u03c1\u03b1 \u03a6\u03c1\u03c5\u03b3\u03af\u03b1\u03c2 (Phrygian Ankyra, i.e. modern Ankara)</a>. The Peutinger Map places it on a route network between \"Mideo\" and \"Pesinvnte\" (i.e., Midaion and <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../609500\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Pessinous</a>). \"<a class=\"geographic\" href=\"http://www.cambridge.org/us/talbert/talbertdatabase/TPPlace2152.html\" id=\"name-3\">Dorileo</a>\" is one route segment leftward of \"Mideo\" on the Peutinger Map; therefore, the <em>BAtlas Directory</em> localizes Trikomia 3 \"between <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../609367\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Dorylaion</a> and Pessinous\".</p>\r\n<p>NB: A <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Tricomia_(Phrygia)&amp;oldid=969487333\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\"><em>Wikipedia</em> entry entitled \"Tricomia (Phrygia)\"</a> conflates this Trikomia with another (<a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../609560\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\"><em>Pleiades</em>\u00a0609560</a>) that may have been located at modern \u0130lkburun in Turkey. Such a view is implicitly rejected by <em>RE</em> and, following it, <em>BAtlas</em> and <em>Pleiades</em>.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "One of several \"Trikomiai\" attested in the ancient Greek and Roman world. This presumed settlement cannot be located today, but probably lay in what is today the country of Turkey, somewhere between Dorylaion (Eski\u015fehir) and Pessinous (Ball\u0131hisar).",
